message: "If you refer to this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SOCL-SNN: Self-Organizing Continual Learning in Spiking Neural Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Lun"
    alias: "liluncoder"
    email: "2381067480@qq.com"
abstract: >-
  An independent research project investigating local learning, synaptic credit
  assignment, temporal information processing, and adaptive mechanisms in spiking neural
  networks. The project studies what a local learning mechanism can represent and carry,
  whether its intervention reaches the weights, and under what conditions network
  structure can adapt without destabilising learning. It is an ongoing experimental
  research project and does not claim general intelligence or open-ended autonomous
  learning.
repository-code: "https://github.com/liluncoder/SOCL-SNN"
url: "https://github.com/liluncoder/SOCL-SNN"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spiking neural networks
  - continual learning
  - credit assignment
  - synaptic plasticity
  - computational neuroscience
  - self-organization
